counterexample:
A bounded loop with delayed attempts, such as an exponentially increasing sleep, is not an immediate retry loop. An error-handling branch that stops on permanent failures and only retries eligible failures with delays and a bound addresses the stronger case.
```rust
let mut delay = Duration::from_millis(100);
for _ in 0..3 {
    match call_external_api().await {
        Ok(res) => return Ok(res),
        Err(_) => {
            tokio::time::sleep(delay).await;
            delay *= 2; // Exponential backoff
        }
    }
}
```

fix:
For immediate dependency retries, insert exponential backoff with random jitter to spread client bursts [39:51]. For unbounded unclassified retries, also classify failures, stop and return permanent errors, cap the delay, and impose a strict maximum retry count, returning the final failure when it is exhausted.
```rust
let mut retries = 0;
loop {
    match connect_to_database("password") {
        Ok(conn) => break Ok(conn),
        Err(e) if e.is_transient() && retries < 5 => {
            sleep(exponential_delay(retries));
            retries += 1;
        }
        Err(e) => break Err(e),
    }
}
```
